    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Gunnar Henderson** stands as our premier offensive anchor. With a robust score of 81.87, he benefits from a favorable matchup against Brown, who carries a shaky 4.53 xERA. **Henderson** is in a prime position to capitalize on his elite platoon advantage, making him our highest-ceiling play. He is flanked by **Sam Antonacci** (67.67) and **Nasim Nunez** (67.37), both of whom are vital to our strategy today. **Antonacci** draws a high-upside matchup against Yesavage, while **Nunez** benefits from a strong park factor and a soft spot against Lopez. These three represent our best combination of raw power and speed-category efficiency, which remains the backbone of the Austin Waves\u2019 roster construction.\n\nWe are navigating a few tactical risks, most notably with **Jackson Merrill** (54.45), who is staring down a 45% rain risk. While his score is bolstered by a solid spot in the order, we are monitoring the weather closely. Our most difficult bench decision was bypassing **Curtis Mead** (58.98). While **Mead** is in a high-scoring environment against Lopez, the optimizer ultimately favored the positional flexibility and defensive floor of **Jacob Wilson** (60.32) in the UTIL spot. We are also sitting **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (54.36) today; despite his pedigree, the matchup against Burke provides a lower efficiency profile compared to the high-volume opportunities afforded to **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, whose matchup against Lopez is projectable for significant volume and scoring potential. We are ready to adjust if late lineup announcements force a change for **Wilson** or **Nunez**.",
